{"id":"59f9509161ed4164023d70b0001072423620d9ad0fff6d10e53b59a4a419faa2","lamport":1,"author":"carlo.cifarelli@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-10-07T21:44:52.616308Z","format_version":1,"kind":"set-field","payload":{"fields":{"description":"## Bug\n\nRunning a scalar mutation (e.g. `ti state closed:wontfix`) on a v1\nplain-field ticket that had never been migrated appended a partial\n`set-field` op at **lamport 0** without first migrating the ticket to v2.\n\n`project_scalar_fields` drops *all* op-managed scalars (title, created-at,\ncreated-by, status, state, …) and re-adds only the fields the op carries.\nA partial set-field op (status/state/closed-by) therefore erases title /\ncreated-at / created-by, so `build_ticket` returns `None` and the ticket\n\"does not project to a valid ticket state\" — `ti show` / `ti checkout` can't\nfind it and `ti verify` flags it. Underlying data (title, description,\ncomments, tags) stays intact in git-meta; only the projection breaks.\n\n## Fix\n\nCommit `ffabd81` — migrate plain-field tickets to v2 (snapshot every scalar\ninto a `Create` op) **before** appending the first op, so the op-log is\nself-contained and partial set-field ops can no longer drop fields.\n\nShipped in **v0.3.2** (bump `dc24720`, pushed to origin/master).\n\n## Field incident (reference)\n\nA real ticket in the `mediaterranea` repo (`c5e6d7`, \"R2 media storage via\nTerraform\") hit this via `ti state closed:wontfix -t c5e6d7` on the old\n0.3.1 binary. Repaired out-of-band: removed the single lamport-0 corrupt op\nvia a `git_meta_lib` `remove()` (tombstone @ now > op ts → wins on merge),\nre-serialized, re-verified (39/39), then closed it cleanly with the fixed\nbinary. No `ti` repair/doctor command exists — manual surgery was required.\n\n## Follow-up (open question)\n\nConsider a built-in `ti` repair/reproject command so future invalid-op-log\ncases don't need manual `git_meta_lib` surgery."}}}